<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liang Hongzhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1946</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liang Hongzhi was a Chinese politician who had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a> before collaborating with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. In March 1938 he became head of the Reformed Government of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, a Japanese-sponsored regime at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>. It was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a>'s government in 1940, and after the war Liang was tried for treason and executed in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liang-hongzhi.jpg" alt="Liang Hongzhi" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown; scanned by 天竺鼠 (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liang_Hongzhi.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
